  "cards": [
    {"dot":"cyan","title":"Turn logic & branches","items":["Intent can end as chat/clarification; tool intent retrieves positive-score BM25 candidates or returns a rephrase request.","Hydrated candidates feed argument generation; eligible names and schemas are validated before sequential MCP calls. No generated calls skips invocation/synthesis.","Successful tool results are validated, then used-tool presentation policies are loaded before answer synthesis."]},
    {"dot":"emerald","title":"Independent cache ownership","items":["Agent SQLite cache stores discovery, index and verified context metadata; it does not cache business results.","MCP server owns the 300-second successful result cache. Calls still cross HTTP on a hit.","A2A card cache is separate; sessions/history are in memory and disappear on process restart."]},
    {"dot":"violet","title":"Model visibility & observability","items":["Retrieval metadata/scores stay host-only. The host projects selected schemas/instructions to argument generation and used-tool policies/results to synthesis.","Trace files can contain user text, arguments and results; context JSONL records exact messages and graph snapshots.","A2A serializes work per context and returns answer/context-trace artifacts; cancellation/failure is surfaced through task status."]}
